const passages={
p1:{title:"Small Changes, Better Study Habits",text:"Many students study for hours without a break, but this does not always help them remember more. A short pause every forty minutes gives the brain time to rest. Students can stand, drink water, or look away from a screen. Keeping phones out of reach may improve concentration. These habits do not replace planning, yet they make study easier to manage. Students who review notes briefly each evening often remember more than those who wait until the night before an exam.",translation:"????????????????????????????????????????????? ?????????????????????????????????? ?????????? ? ??????????????????????????? ?????????? ??????? ??????????????????? ???????????????????????????????????? ?????????????????????????????? ??????????????????????????? ???????????????????????????????????????????????????????????"},
p2:{title:"Why Cities Need Trees",text:"Trees do more than make a city attractive. Their leaves provide shade and can lower sidewalk temperatures. Trees absorb some rainwater, helping reduce floods after storms. Parks with trees give residents a place to walk and meet neighbors. However, city trees need regular care. Young trees must be watered, and branches may need trimming near power lines. Planting is only the first step; communities must protect and maintain the trees.",translation:"??????????????????????????????? ??????????????????????????????? ????????????????????????????????????? ????????????????????????????? ???????????? ????????????????????? ???????????????? ?????????????????????????? ?????????????????? ???????????????????????????"},
p3:{title:"A Library of Things",text:"A neighborhood library now lends tools such as drills, sewing machines, and gardening equipment. Many people need these items only once or twice a year, so buying one for every home can be wasteful. Members reserve an item online and return it after use. The library saves money and keeps useful objects from being thrown away. Weekend workshops teach repair skills. Some tools require special training, so the library checks each item before lending it.",translation:"??????????????????????????????????? ???? ????? ??????????? ????????????? ?????????????????????????????????????????????? ??????????????????????????? ????????????????????????????? ????????????????????????????????????????? ?????????????????????? ???????????????????????????? ????????????????????????????"},
p4:{title:"Sleep and Memory",text:"Sleep plays an important role in learning. During sleep, the brain organizes daily information and strengthens some memories. A student who studies late but sleeps only a few hours may struggle to focus the next morning. Experts recommend a regular bedtime and a quiet, dark bedroom. They also suggest avoiding bright screens before sleep. These habits cannot guarantee a perfect score, but they support attention and memory. A good study plan should include enough sleep, not only extra textbook hours.",translation:"??????????????????????????? ????????????????????????????????????? ??????????????????????????????????????????????????????? ???????????????????????????????? ??????????????? ??????????????????????????????? ?????????????????????????????? ????????????????????? ??????????????????????????"},
p5:{title:"Restoring a Coral Reef",text:"Coral reefs shelter sea animals and protect coastlines from waves. Warmer water has damaged coral in some areas, so local teams are testing restoration. Divers collect small pieces from healthy coral and attach them to underwater frames. The frames are checked regularly, and damaged pieces are replaced. Restoration can help, but it cannot solve every problem. Pollution and excessive fishing must also be controlled. Scientists work with residents and officials to protect the wider marine environment.",translation:"???????????????????????????????????????????????????????????? ?????????????????????????????? ????????????????????????? ???????????????????????????????????????????????????????????????? ???????????????????????????????????? ???????????????????????????????????????? ???????????????????????????????????????????????"},
p6:{title:"Learning to Use Public Transport",text:"A city introduced a travel card for buses, trains, and ferries. Passengers can change services without buying a separate ticket each time. Some older residents found the system confusing, so help desks opened at busy stations. Staff taught people how to add money and check a balance. Later, more residents used public transport for short trips. The city still needs more frequent service in distant neighborhoods, but the card has made transfers easier.",translation:"????????????????????????????????????????? ???? ??????? ???????????????????????????????????????????? ??????????????????????????????????????????????????? ???????????????????????????????? ????????????????????????????????????? ????????????????????????????????? ??????????????????????????????"}
};
